{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/414712-houserule-to-make-tactics-actually-useful","id":414712,"title":"Houserule to Make Tactics Actually Useful","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-21T18:27:03-08:00","id":414712,"title":"Houserule to Make Tactics Actually Useful","content":"I spent a lot of time pouring over the rules for Tactics since Hunter came out, trying to find anything that makes them different from the standard teamwork rule. There isn't. It's just something to sink Practical Experience into for no reason. The book describes them, however, as maneuvers that the cell has practiced so much that it's like second nature. That got me thinking about how to fix Tactics to make it worth the PXP investment.<br /> <br /> When the cell spends PXP to buy a Tactic, you assign specific PCs to the roles of the Tactic. If the cell performs the Tactic with the right people in the right positions, everyone gets the Rote quality on their rolls. <br /> <br /> Example: Staking.<br /> John is assigned to the primary Strength + Weaponry roll.<br /> Alan and Peter are assigned to the secondary Strength + Brawl rolls.<br /> Billy is assigned to the secondary Wits + Medicine roll.<br /> If John, Alan, Peter, and Billy all do their assigned jobs within the Tactic, they all get Rote on their rolls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2573-inkpenavenger","name":"inkpenavenger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2573_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T14:35:10-08:00","id":417977,"title":"","content":"Interesting...<br /> <br /> Mind if I include it in my rules for <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/362783-gmc-freeform-tactics\">Freeform Tactics</a>? It would give more of a reason to actually buy a Tactic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T15:28:28-08:00","id":418033,"title":"","content":"Why not just remove XP costs from tactics and let these be things that any sufficiently skilled cell can do?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T16:01:08-08:00","id":418056,"title":"","content":"I always thought the point was that tactics let you do things that you just plain can't do without a tactic. I.E. reliably incite a werewolf into Death Rage, and additionally have a chance of making it so the werewolf ONLY attacks its own pack, not you. Another one lets you apparently nullify the werewolf's scent powers, even if they have tasted blood... That is, it's a teamwork-based superpower that's at least nominally non-magical. <br /> <br /> If it's something that doesn't seem powerful enough to you to justify the exp, maybe just expand on what it does a little. That, or re-examine just what kinds of ridiculous things you're letting players do as routine actions if you let them punch the fangs out of vampires as standard brawl attacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","name":"Wraith_Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}